l</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Enlil was the chief god of the Sumerian pantheon, lord of the wind and air, whose temple, the Ekur, stood at Nippur.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enlil-bani"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enlil-bani.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enlil-bani</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enlil-bani was a king of the Isin dynasty in Mesopotamia in the 19th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enlil-nadin-ahi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enlil-nadin-ahi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enlil-nadin-ahi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enlil-nadin-ahi was the last king of the Kassite dynasty of Babylonia, ruling for about three years in the mid-12th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enmebaragesi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enmebaragesi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enmebaragesi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enmebaragesi was a king of Kish who lived around 2700 BCE and is one of the earliest Mesopotamian rulers attested in inscriptions.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enmerkar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enmerkar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enmerkar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enmerkar was a legendary king of Uruk, listed in the Sumerian King List and remembered in Sumerian epic poems as a son of the sun god Utu.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enmetena"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enmetena.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enmetena</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enmetena was a ruler of the Sumerian city-state of Lagash around 2400 BCE and a nephew of Eannatum.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/enna-cennselach"><span class="enc-name">Énna Cennselach</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Énna Cennselach was a king of Leinster in early medieval Ireland, said to have lived in the 5th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/enna-dagan"><span class="enc-name">Enna-Dagan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Enna-Dagan was a king of Mari on the Euphrates in the twenty-fourth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ennis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ennis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ennis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ennis is the county town of County Clare in the west of Ireland, on the River Fergus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enniskillen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enniskillen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enniskillen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Enniskillen is the county town of Fermanagh in Northern Ireland, on an island between Upper and Lower Lough Erne.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/enniskillen-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enniskillen-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Enniskillen Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Enniskillen Castle is a castle in Enniskillen, County Fermanagh, built by the Maguire lords of Fermana